      "description": "Note: You can easily convert this markdown file to a PDF in VSCode using this handy extension Markdown PDF.\nBack to the Top\nWindows Terminal is a new, modern, feature-rich, productive terminal application for command-line users. It includes many of the features most frequently requested by the Windows command-line community including support for tabs, rich text, globalization, configurability, theming & styling, and more. Take a look at the Windows Terminal GitHub.\nGit for Windows is a distributed version control system tool that focuses on offering a lightweight, native set of tools that bring the full feature set of the Git SCM to Windows while providing appropriate user interfaces for experienced Git users and novices alike.\nWindows UI Library (WinUI) is a native user experience (UX) framework for both Windows desktop and UWP applications. Take a look at the Windows UI Library Roadmap.\nWindows UI Library (WinUI) 2 is tightly integrated with Windows 10 and later SDKs and provides official native Windows UI controls and other user interface elements for UWP applications (and desktop applications using XAML Islands).\nXAML Islands) is a feature that enables you to enhance the look, feel, and functionality of your existing WPF, Windows Forms, and C++ desktop (Win32) applications with the latest Windows 10 UI features that are only available via WinRT XAML controls. This means that you can use UWP features such as Windows Ink and controls that support the Fluent Design System in your existing WPF, Windows Forms, and C++ desktop applications.\nWindows Community Toolkit is a collection of helper functions, custom controls, and app services. It simplifies and demonstrates common developer tasks building UWP apps for Windows 10. The toolkit can be used to build apps for any Windows 10 device, including PC, Mobile, Xbox, IoT and HoloLens. You can also use the toolkit with an existing desktop app converted to UWP using the Desktop Bridge.\nWindows Pseudo Console (ConPTY) is an API that provides a mechanism that is similar to the POSIX PTY model, but in a Windows-relevant manner VT Interactivity. Where it receives incoming UTF-8 encoded text, converts each displayable text character into the corresponding INPUT_RECORD, and stores them in the Input Buffer.\nComparison of WinUI 3 and WinUI 2\nIntroducing Windows Terminal\nAn overview on Windows Terminal | Microsoft Docs\nWindows Terminal Actions | Microsoft Docs\nWindows Terminal command line arguments | Microsoft Docs\nWindows Terminal SSH | Microsoft Docs\nWindows Terminal Themes\nTop Windows Command Line Courses Online | Udemy\nLearning Windows Terminal Online Class | LinkedIn Learning\nLearning the Command Line with Online Courses | edX",
